Line 2 "t.list <- paste0(UG.UQ.list[,1],"",1:4366)" is not needed in your code. This was used to generate a tree in the example case.

In the grp list, you can use your own data table. But the format of your data is not clear. I can't give you more suggestions.
Here is an example that is closer to your situation.

# a random tree
tree <- rtree(10)

# show tip label of tree
tree$tip.label

# group tip label
grp <- list(UG = tree$tip.label[1:5],
            UQ = tree$tip.label[6:10])

# or in this way
# grp <- list(UG = c("t7", "t6", "t4", "t1", "t3"),
#             UQ = c("t9",  "t2",  "t5",  "t8",  "t10"))

# plot tree
tree_plot <- ggtree(tree, layout = 'circular', branch.length='none')

# group color
groupOTU(tree_plot, grp, 'Species') + aes(color=Species) +
  theme(legend.position="right")

