It is possible, but we didn't provide direct support to visualize the map.

Currently, you can parse a SIMMAP file using phytools, http://www.phytools.org/static.help/read.simmap.html, and visualize tree structure using ggtree.

Maybe we can develop an as.treedata method for SIMMAP, http://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/chapter1.html#as-treedata

